<title>UK: SOCCER-QUALIFIERS FOR EUROPEAN CLUB QUARTER-FINALS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-QUALIFIERS FOR EUROPEAN CLUB QUARTER-FINALS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four teams from Spain have qualified for the quarter-finals of the three European Club competitions -- the European Cup (EC), Cup Winners' Cup (CWC) and UEFA Cup.</p>
<p>Country-by-country representation in next March's quarter-finals:</p>
<p>			 EC	    CWC	     UEFA</p>
<p> 4-Spain	  Atl Madrid  Barcelona     Tenerife</p>
<p>							Valencia</p>
<p> 3-England	Man Utd     Liverpool     Newcastle</p>
<p> 3-France	 Auxerre     Paris St G    Monaco</p>
<p> 3-Italy	  Juventus    Fiorentina    Inter Milan</p>
<p> 2-Germany	B Dortmund		    Schalke</p>
<p> 2-Norway	 Rosenborg   Brann Bergen</p>
<p> 2-Portugal     Porto	 Benfica</p>
<p> 1-Netherlands  Ajax</p>
<p> 1-Greece			 AEK Athens</p>
<p> 1-Sweden			 AIK Stockholm</p>
<p> 1-Belgium					  Anderlecht</p>
<p> 1-Denmark					  Brondby</p>
</text>
